+retries. This uses no separate per-message authorization ledger.
+
+Grant provenance uses each accepted human entry's validated metadata.mode, never the module
+scope: Base may fold several queued entries before notifying hooks, so the final batch mode
+cannot authorize earlier entries. Missing or invalid per-entry modes leave the previous human
+grant unchanged. The real human API enqueue transaction records one pending restriction per
+agent; every collaboration selection, including a model switch, is capped until acceptance. A
+later human Full enqueue clears that cap but does not create a grant before acceptance. Agent
+and guest messages cannot create or clear it. Existing-ID delivery retries never rewrite lastMode.
+
+An accepted-message hook already runs inside its agent's operation. Calling updateMetadata on
